## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a simple, scalable ingestion path with clear isolation and observable state using familiar GCP primitives.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub streaming ingestion
- Cloud Run consumer with auto-scaling
- Idempotent processing via Pub/Sub message_id and an idempotence store
- Per-tenant isolation using separate BigQuery datasets
- Least-privilege IAM, Cloud Logging/Monitoring
- Basic test plan with replay and failure injection

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-handler showing idempotent check
async function handle(msg) {
  const id = msg.message_id;
  if (await isProcessed(id)) return;
  await enrichAndStore(msg);
  await markProcessed(id);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle backpressure if tenants spike?
- What changes to support a new tenant without code redeployments?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a production-grade multi-tenant pipeline with strict data isolation, governance, and cost controls across GCP services, plus a robust testing and rollback strategy.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant data isolation with per-tenant Cloud Storage and per-tenant BigQuery datasets
- Dataflow pipeline correctness, idempotence, and scheduling
- IAM and IAM Conditions for least privilege
- Cross-region DR, data residency, and backup strategy
- Cost visibility with labels and budgets

## Code Example

```javascript
class ValidateAndEnrich {
  process(element) {
    if (!valid_schema(element)) return;
    const enriched = enrich(element);
    return enriched;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle schema changes across tenants without downtime?
- How do you enforce per-tenant security boundaries in a shared data lake?

